ated to courses taught. Some disciplines require discipline specific certifications and/or licensure in the field for practice or functioning within the State of Illinois; degree specific course work and/or graduate degrees in the discipline. Responsibilities include teaching undergraduate and graduate level courses in the field of Bilingual Education and second language acquisition including foundations, assessment, methods, cross cultural, linguistics and best practices in both face to face and online formats, and collaborating on program development including course refinement, and assessment. Required Education MA in Education Required Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Expertise and solid knowledge base in areas of teaching as well as proficiency in speaking and writing Spanish; a minimum of 3 years teaching experience in urban/suburban elementary bilingual programs and multicultural settings. Preferred Qualifications Doctorate in Curriculum and Instruction, Bilingual Education or related field preferred Posting Information Open Date 02/21/2025 Close Date 06/30/2025 Pass Message Fail Message Special Instructions to Applicants Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae References Optional Documents If you are interested in attending CSU, please complete our graduate or undergraduate form, and we will send you admissions information. Copyright © 2009 All Rights Reserved. Chicago State University | 9501 South King Drive, Chicago, Illinois 60628-1598 | (773) 995-2000 Emergency and Weather Updates | Swine Flu Updates | Exercise Your Right to Vote | Higher Learning Commission Mark of Affiliation | Campus Security Report | Whistle Blower Protections | Report A Site Problem | For Those With Disabilities | The university's policy is to be in full compliance with all federal and state nondiscrimination and equal opportunity laws, orders and regulations. Privacy Policy | 