    "https://chicagostate.peopleadmin.com/postings/16143": {
      "title": "Chicago State University Applicant Portal Site | Clinical Assistant Professor/ 12 Month",
      "description": "Chicago State University Applicant Portal Site | Clinical Assistant Professor/ 12 Month Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Clinical Assistant Professor/ 12 Month Bookmark this Hiring-Authorization Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number F250033P Open Date 06/24/2025 Close Date Faculty Rank Assistant Professor Title Clinical Assistant Professor/ 12 Month Salary $110,000 – $114,562 Annual Benefits This position is eligible for health, dental, life insurance and other benefits through Chicago State University. Click here for a complete list of benefits: https://csu.edu/humanresources/benefits.htm Is Tenured/ Tenure Track No Full-time/ Part-time Full-time Job Description Summary Chicago State University ( CSU ), is the oldest public university in the Chicago metropolitan area. Chicago State University is Illinois’ only four-year U.S. Department of Education-designated Predominantly Black Institution ( PBI ). CSU serves over 1,500 undergraduate students and nearly 900 graduate students. The university is a nationally accredited university with five colleges in Arts and Sciences, Business, Education, Health Sciences and Pharmacy and proudly supports a diverse and non-traditional student population that hails from 28 countries and 36 states. Discover the latest advancements and milestones achieved by CSU in our Annual Report : https://www.csu.edu/president/annual_report.htm . Chicago State University School of Pharmacy ( CSU - SOP ) invites applications for the following faculty position. The successful applicant will serve as part of a multidisciplinary team with the opportunity to participate in the continued growth and development of the college of pharmacy and clinical practice site. Academic rank and salary will be commensurate with experience. A non-tenure track, calendar year pharmacy practice faculty position is available in Internal Medicine. Responsibilities include didactic and experiential teaching, practice site development, scholarship and participation in the service missions of the college. The preferred candidate will have a Pharm.D. with advanced residency training or the equivalent, the ability to develop an innovative pharmacy practice and conduct collaborative research, evidence of teaching experience and be eligible for Illinois state licensure. Discover the latest advancements and milestones achieved by CSU in our Annual Report : https://www.csu.edu/president/annual_report.htm . Required Education Qualified applicants should be eligible for Illinois state licensure and possess a PharmD with advanced residency and/or fellowship training or equivalent experience. Required Knowledge, Skills and Abilities All candidates should exhibit strong verbal and written communication, organizational and interpersonal skills. In addition, a commitment to student-centered education and demonstrable promotion and enhancement of diversity is required. Preferred Qualifications Candidates with advanced residency (PGY2) are preferred. Experience in using modern teaching approaches that incorporate active learning is desirable. Experience working with students from diverse backgrounds is preferred. Special Requirements Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is the highest level of education attained? GED High School Diploma Associates Degree Bachelors Degree Masters Degree PHD * How many years of experience do you have in this type of position? 0-1 1-3 3-5 5-7 7+ * Do you agree to a criminal background check? Yes No * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Indeed Linkedin HigherEd Jobs CSU Website Personal referral Website Advertisement/Publication Other Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae List of (3) References Optional Documents Teaching Philosophy If you are interested in attending CSU, please complete our graduate or undergraduate form, and we will send you admissions information. Copyright © 2009 All Rights Reserved. Chicago State University | 9501 South King Drive, Chicago, Illinois 60628-1598 | (773) 995-2000 Emergency and Weather Updates | Swine Flu Updates | Exercise Your Right to Vote | Higher Learning Commission Mark of Affiliation | Campus Security Report | Whistle Blower Protections | Report A Site Problem | For Those With Disabilities | The university's policy is to be in full compliance with all federal and state nondiscrimination and equal opportunity laws, orders and regulations. Privacy Policy | Chicago State University is an Equal Opportunity/ Affirmative Action Employer (PDF) | These pages are best viewed with Internet Explorer 7, Netscape 7.1, Firefox 3.5.x, Safari 3.1.2, Chrome 3.0.1 and later browsers. | Undergraduate Admissions' Information | Exercise Your Right to Vote To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://chicagostate.peopleadmin.com/pools/15861": {
      "title": "Chicago State University Applicant Portal Site",
      "description": "Chicago State University Applicant Portal Site Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Part-Time Lecturer (Geography) (Pool) Bookmark this Pool | Print Preview | Apply for this Pool Pool Details Pool Information for the Posting Pool Number Pool Name Part-Time Lecturer (Geography) Faculty Rank Lecturer Class Code C6139 Is Tenured/ Tenure Track No Full-time/ Part-time Part-time Job Description Summary The budgeted salary for this position is typically $1,000 per credit hour . This position is ineligible for health, dental, and life insurance benefits through Chicago State University. Chicago State University ( CSU ), is the oldest public university in the Chicago metropolitan area. Chicago State University is Illinois’ only four-year U.S. Department of Education-designated Predominantly Black Institution ( PBI ). CSU serves over 1,500 undergraduate students and nearly 900 graduate students. The university is a nationally accredited university with five colleges in Arts and Sciences, Business, Education, Health Sciences and Pharmacy and proudly supports a diverse and non-traditional student population that hails from 28 countries and 36 states. Discover the latest advancements and milestones achieved by CSU in our Annual Report : https://www.csu.edu/president/annual_report.htm . All faculty positions are governed by the tenets of a collective bargaining agreement. Faculty are hired, evaluated, and retained on the basis of conditions covered in the union contract. Primary duties include teaching and related activities assigned during a term of 4.5 months. It is expected that each faculty member engages in teaching and teaching-related activities. Non-tenure track faculty report to a department chairperson or director. Teaching: faculty members are expected to teach; develop syllabi and teaching materials (ability to organize, analyze, and present knowledge or materials) related to courses taught. Some disciplines require discipline specific certifications and/or licensure in the field for practice or functioning within the State of Illinois; degree specific course work and/or graduate degrees in the discipline. Required Education MA in geography required, ABD or PhD welcomed. Required Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Ability to teach introductory level and general geography courses. Ability to teach students who come from diverse educational and social backgrounds. Preferred Qualifications Previous teaching experience not required but welcome Posting Information Open Date 02/21/2025 Close Date 06/30/2025 Pass Message Fail Message Special Instructions to Applicants Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents If you are interested in attending CSU, please complete our graduate or undergraduate form, and we will send you admissions information. Copyright © 2009 All Rights Reserved. Chicago State University | 9501 South King Drive, Chicago, Illinois 60628-1598 | (773) 995-2000 Emergency and Weather Updates | Swine Flu Updates | Exercise Your Right to Vote | Higher Learning Commission Mark of Affiliation | Campus Security Report | Whistle Blower Protections | Report A Site Problem | For Those With Disabilities | The university's policy is to be in full compliance with all federal and state nondiscrimination and equal opportunity laws, orders and regulations. Privacy Policy | Chicago State University is an Equal Opportunity/ Affirmative Action Employer (PDF) | These pages are best viewed with Internet Explorer 7, Netscape 7.1, Firefox 3.5.x, Safari 3.1.2, Chrome 3.0.1 and later browsers. | Undergraduate Admissions' Information | Exercise Your Right to Vote To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://chicagostate.peopleadmin.com/postings/17026": {
      "title": "Chicago State University Applicant Portal Site | Infant-ToddlerTwos Assistant Teacher",
      "description": "Chicago State University Applicant Portal Site | Infant-ToddlerTwos Assistant Teacher Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Infant-ToddlerTwos Assistant Teacher Bookmark this Hiring-Authorization Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number S27393P Posting Date Closing Date Title Child Development Associate Working Title Infant-ToddlerTwos Assistant Teacher Salary Range $20.51 Per Hour / $40,000 Annual Employee Class Civil Service Department Office of the Dean of Education Full-time/ Part-time Full-time Specialization Hours Per Week 37.5 Standard Work Week Monday - Friday Benefits This position is eligible for health, dental, life insurance and other benefits through Chicago State University. Click here for a complete list of benefits: https://csu.edu/humanresources/benefits.htm Job Summary The IT2 Assistant Teacher position works in a collaborative co-teaching team model to provide high quality early care and learning experiences to children 3 months – 3 years old. In this role the person under the guidance of the teams lead plans and implements curriculum. Supports the implementation and completion of child development screenings and assessments. Engage in all family engagement activities such as home visits, conferences, etc. Adhere, to all licensing, funding and accreditation standards and compliance. Maintain, a safe, health nurturing and developmentally appropriate environment. Job Description Job Duties – Assistant Teacher (Infant/Toddler/Two-Year-Old Classroom) Collaborate with the lead teacher and co-teaching team to plan and implement developmentally appropriate curriculum and daily learning activities for children ages 3 months to 3 years. Support the delivery of high-quality early care and learning experiences that promote children’s social, emotional, cognitive, language, and physical development. Assist in observing children and documenting developmental progress to support ongoing assessments and child development screenings. Contribute to the implementation and completion of required child development screenings and assessments in collaboration with the teaching team. Foster warm, responsive relationships with children through nurturing interactions, positive guidance, and attentive care giving routines. Assist with daily classroom routines including feeding, diapering, toileting, napping, and transitions while promoting children’s independence and well-being. Maintain a safe, clean, healthy, and developmentally appropriate classroom environment that supports active learning and exploration. Ensure all classroom practices comply with licensing regulations, program funding requirements, and accreditation standards. Support family engagement by participating in activities such as parent conferences, home visits, and family events as directed by the teaching team. Communicate respectfully and effectively with families to support children’s learning and development. Prepare and organize classroom materials, learning centers, and activities that reflect the planned curriculum. Work collaboratively with team members and program staff to maintain consistent classroom practices and a positive learning environment. Participate in required trainings, meetings, and professional development opportunities to enhance early childhood teaching practices. Follow program policies and procedures related to health, safety, supervision, and child protection. May be assigned as the temporary team lead in absence of the lead. Other duties as assigned an appropriate to the overall success of the program. Minimum Qualifications CREDENTIALS TO BE VERIFIED BY PLACEMENT OFFICER Possession of credentials required by Illinois Department of Children and Family Services for employment as a Child Care Worker in a licensed child care facility. The Illinois Department of Children and Family Services required credentials can be reviewed at: http://www.ilga.gov/commission/jcar/admincode/089/089004070D01400R.html KNOWLEDGE , SKILLS AND ABILITIES (KSAs) physical examination as required by Illinois Child Care Act for employees in child care facilities personal attributes required by Illinois Department of Children and Family Services for all child care personnel Preferred Qualifications 60 semester or 90 quarter hours (from accredited college or university) With 6 semester or 9 quarter credit hours in ECE , child development ot related course work. Must have or be working towards a IL Gateway Level 4 IT credentia l as indicated on IL Gateway PDR . . Have at least 1 year experience working with children birth – 5 years old Alternatively: Have a High School/ GED with a valid Infant Toddler CDA . Must have or be working towards a IL Gateway Level 2 IT credential as indicated on IL Gateway PDR . 1 year experience working with children birth – 5 years old. Associate Degree in ECE or Child Development with a Level 4 IL Gateway IT credential. 3 years experience in working with children birth – 5 in a child care or school setting. 1 year experience as an Early Head Start teacher. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Meet all University and DCFS hiring requirements, including background check and -Physical Examination Follow all IDEC ? DCFS licensing guidelines and Head Start Performance Standards Attend required training and professional development Additional Applicant Information Physical Requirement/ Demands The role requires significant physical stamina, with long periods of standing, walkingand regularly lifting and moving items. Must be able to physically interact with children, including talk, hear, sit, stand, walk; use hands to finger, handle or feel objects, tools, or controls; reach with hands and arms; and stoop, kneel, crouch,or crawl and lift and or move items of up to 40 pounds Work Environment Typical early childhood center classroom environment. Classroom are designed to be child centered with child size furnished and equipment per developmentally appropriate per age group. Outdoor spaces with child size equipment and campus walks as permissible per weather and/or safety conditions. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Do you have an Illinois Gateway Infant-Toddler credential? Yes No Do you have experience working with young children birth-3 years old? (Open Ended Question) Do you agree to a IL DCFS background check that includes finger printing, criminal history, child abuse and neglect, sex offender and possible FBI check? Yes No Do you have experience working in Early/Head Start? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of (3) References Optional Documents Transcripts Certification If you are interested in attending CSU, please complete our graduate or undergraduate form, and we will send you admissions information. Copyright © 2009 All Rights Reserved. Chicago State University | 9501 South King Drive, Chicago, Illinois 60628-1598 | (773) 995-2000 Emergency and Weather Updates | Swine Flu Updates | Exercise Your Right to Vote | Higher Learning Commission Mark of Affiliation | Campus Security Report | Whistle Blower Protections | Report A Site Problem | For Those With Disabilities | The university's policy is to be in full compliance with all federal and state nondiscrimination and equal opportunity laws, orders and regulations. Privacy Policy | Chicago State University is an Equal Opportunity/ Affirmative Action Employer (PDF) | These pages are best viewed with Internet Explorer 7, Netscape 7.1, Firefox 3.5.x, Safari 3.1.2, Chrome 3.0.1 and later browsers. | Undergraduate Admissions' Information | Exercise Your Right to Vote To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://chicagostate.peopleadmin.com/pools/15888": {
      "title": "Chicago State University Applicant Portal Site",
      "description": "Chicago State University Applicant Portal Site Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Nontraditional Programs and Continuing Education - Adjunct Lecture (Pool) Bookmark this Pool | Print Preview | Apply for this Pool Pool Details Pool Information for the Posting Pool Number Pool Name Nontraditional Programs and Continuing Education - Adjunct Lecture Faculty Rank Lecturer Class Code Is Tenured/ Tenure Track No Full-time/ Part-time Part-time Job Description Summary The budgeted salary for this position is typically $1,000 per credit hour . This position is ineligible for health, dental, and life insurance benefits through Chicago State University. Chicago State University ( CSU ), is the oldest public university in the Chicago metropolitan area. Chicago State University is Illinois’ only four-year U.S. Department of Education-designated Predominantly Black Institution ( PBI ). CSU serves over 1,500 undergraduate students and nearly 900 graduate students. The university is a nationally accredited university with five colleges in Arts and Sciences, Business, Education, Health Sciences and Pharmacy and proudly supports a diverse and non-traditional student population that hails from 28 countries and 36 states. Discover the latest advancements and milestones achieved by CSU in our Annual Report : https://www.csu.edu/president/annual_report.htm . The Adjunct faculty member will serve as a key team member in the Division of Nontraditional Programs and Continuing Education. The candidate will use a variety of instructional methods to teach and assess students. • Develop course curriculum. • Create a course syllabus for each class they teach. • Attend required training for academic advisors • Deliver and lead discussions for the course they are assigned to teach. • Collaborate with other professors to create coursework. • Schedule and facilitate Program Majors meetings • Assist in recruiting and marketing. • Select and implement a variety of instructional material. • Evaluate student learning outcomes. • Maintain accurate records of a student’s academic progress. • Be accessible to students via phone, academic advising hours, LMS , Zoom and email. • Participate in all mandatory training offered by the university. • Participate in professional development opportunities. • Engage students in and outside of class. • Adhere to all university policies and requirements. • Adhere to all other duties as assigned. Required Education Master’s Degree in education or similar field. Required Knowledge, Skills and Abilities • Possess strong communication and presentation skills. • Possess strong technical skills. • Possess a working knowledge of using a Learning Management System (Moodle, Canvas, Blackboard) to teach, engage and assess students. • Possess excellent interpersonal and communication skills. • Possess teaching experience at the post-secondary level or higher. • Possess good time management skills. Preferred Qualifications • Possess three more years teaching at the Community College or higher. • Possess an active research agenda in the field of Adult Education. Posting Information Open Date 02/21/2025 Close Date 06/30/2025 Pass Message Fail Message Special Instructions to Applicants Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Transcripts Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter References Certification Letters of Reference Sample of Teaching Evaluation Writing Sample If you are interested in attending CSU, please complete our graduate or undergraduate form, and we will send you admissions information. Copyright © 2009 All Rights Reserved. Chicago State University | 9501 South King Drive, Chicago, Illinois 60628-1598 | (773) 995-2000 Emergency and Weather Updates | Swine Flu Updates | Exercise Your Right to Vote | Higher Learning Commission Mark of Affiliation | Campus Security Report | Whistle Blower Protections | Report A Site Problem | For Those With Disabilities | The university's policy is to be in full compliance with all federal and state nondiscrimination and equal opportunity laws, orders and regulations. Privacy Policy | Chicago State University is an Equal Opportunity/ Affirmative Action Employer (PDF) | These pages are best viewed with Internet Explorer 7, Netscape 7.1, Firefox 3.5.x, Safari 3.1.2, Chrome 3.0.1 and later browsers. | Undergraduate Admissions' Information | Exercise Your Right to Vote To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
