    "https://chicagostate.peopleadmin.com/postings/17006": {
      "title": "Chicago State University Applicant Portal Site | Women&#39;s Assistant Track and Field /Cross Country Coach",
      "description": "Chicago State University Applicant Portal Site | Women&#39;s Assistant Track and Field /Cross Country Coach Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Women's Assistant Track and Field /Cross Country Coach Bookmark this Hiring-Authorization Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number S27390P Posting Date 07/20/2026 Closing Date Title Women's Assistant Track and Field and Cross Country Coach Working Title Women's Assistant Track and Field /Cross Country Coach Salary Range 10,000 Annual Employee Class Temporary Assignment Department Athletics Full-time/ Part-time Part-time Specialization Temporary Hours Per Week 20-25 Standard Work Week Monday- Friday with occasional evenings and weekends Benefits Not Applicable Job Summary Reporting to the Director of Track and Field & Cross Country Coach, The Assistant Track and Field & Cross Country Coach , manages and coordinates all operations related to the Distance program including but not limited to practice management, development of program, traveling to meets, meeting with student athletes, meeting recruits and communicating with the Director of Track & Field and Cross Country. Job Description 1. Coordinate, Develop and implement practice plan 2. Drive student athletes to practices and Meets 3. Travel to Cross Country and Track & Field Meets 4. Coordinate, and Develop strategic strategies for Distance & Cross Country Athletes 5. Maintain CARA Logs for Distance Athletes 6. Participate in recruiting distance prospects 7. Ability to communicate the standards and uphold expectations of the program Minimum Qualifications CREDENTIALS TO BE VERIFIED BY PLACEMENT OFFICER ● Bachelor’s degree ● USATF Cross Country Specialist ● USTF Level 1 coach or Similar certification ● 2 or more years of paid coaching experience Must have and maintain a valid driver’s license and comply with the University’s vehicle use policy Preferred Qualifications One year or more coaching experience as High School or College Coach Gait Analysis Performance experience Familiar with managing/ administration of NCAA rules and regulations. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities ● Knowledge of recruitment practices. ● Knowledge of social media analytics, social media publishing tools, web analytics, and tracking technologies. ● Knowledge of Microsoft Office suites ● Coordination and Facilitation of Student Athlete Meetings and Academic supervision ● Knowledge of Mid Distance and Distance Training. ● Skill in managing effective communication for a group of Student Athletes ● Implement and develop effect training plans for Mid Distance and Distance athletes ● Implement and Develop communication for practice plans, travel and academic information ● Ability to develop and execute Mid Distance, Distance and Cross Country workouts Additional Applicant Information Physical Requirement/ Demands ●Demonstrated ability to clearly communicate verbally, read, write, see, and hear to perform essential functions. ●Frequent bending, reaching, lifting, pushing, and pulling up to 30 pounds. ●Demonstrate ability to drive vans for Travel Meets that are required for meets ●Prolonged standing at athletic contests and events. Work Environment ● Indoor and outdoor working environment in all weather conditions ● Ability to drive a van ●Non-traditional hours will be required ● Travel to designated away events required ______________________________________________________________________________________ Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter If you are interested in attending CSU, please complete our graduate or undergraduate form, and we will send you admissions information. Copyright © 2009 All Rights Reserved. Chicago State University | 9501 South King Drive, Chicago, Illinois 60628-1598 | (773) 995-2000 Emergency and Weather Updates | Swine Flu Updates | Exercise Your Right to Vote | Higher Learning Commission Mark of Affiliation | Campus Security Report | Whistle Blower Protections | Report A Site Problem | For Those With Disabilities | The university's policy is to be in full compliance with all federal and state nondiscrimination and equal opportunity laws, orders and regulations. Privacy Policy | Chicago State University is an Equal Opportunity/ Affirmative Action Employer (PDF) | These pages are best viewed with Internet Explorer 7, Netscape 7.1, Firefox 3.5.x, Safari 3.1.2, Chrome 3.0.1 and later browsers. | Undergraduate Admissions' Information | Exercise Your Right to Vote To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
