    "https://chicagostate.peopleadmin.com/postings/17012": {
      "title": "Chicago State University Applicant Portal Site",
      "description": "Chicago State University Applicant Portal Site | Deputy Chief of Staff Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Deputy Chief of Staff Bookmark this Hiring-Authorization Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number S26381P Posting Date Closing Date Title Deputy Chief of Staff Working Title Deputy Chief of Staff Salary Range $70,000-84,000 Annually Employee Class Administrator Department Communication & External Relations Full-time/ Part-time Full-time Specialization At least three years of demonstrated experience in leading complex, cross-functional projects related to community, government, or corporate partnerships At least two years of demonstrated experience in managing grants, including overseeing budgets and project implementation Hours Per Week 40 Standard Work Week Monday-Friday Benefits This position is eligible for health, dental, life insurance and other benefits through Chicago State University. Click here for a complete list of benefits: https://csu.edu/humanresources/benefits.htm Job Summary The Deputy Chief of Staff provides strategic, operational, and project management leadership to the University’s Office of External Affairs. Reporting to the Senior Vice President of External Affairs & Strategic Initiatives, this individual is the second-most senior member of the Department of External Affairs. This role drives the advancement of the University’s public mission by coordinating legislative priorities, external relations, and advancement initiatives in alignment with state, system, and institutional goals. The position serves as a trusted advisor to senior leadership and a central coordinator across academic, administrative, and external stakeholders—ensuring initiatives are executed efficiently, compliantly, and with appropriate public accountability. Job Description Project & Initiative Execution and Management Lead and manage complex, cross-functional initiatives related to government relations, public funding, capital projects, and institutional advancement. Develop and maintain project plans, timelines, and performance metrics for high-priority initiatives, including legislative strategies and public-facing campaigns. Identify risks, dependencies, and compliance considerations; proactively address challenges to ensure timely and effective outcomes. Coordinate messaging and outreach efforts to ensure consistency across government affairs, advancement, communications, and academic units Key bodies of work include: Government Affairs: Support state, federal, and local government relations efforts, including policy analysis and stakeholder engagement, particularly supporting our federal engagement strategy and the National Coalition of Predominantly Black Institutions. Partnership & Advancement: The Deputy Chief of Staff will spearhead the university’s partnership strategy, including owning the creation and management of a partnership strategy for the university and the success of several highly visible and complex relationships. This work will include working across the university to create relationships that fully benefit the university and our community. Event Czar: The Office of External Affairs hosts over a dozen highly visible, complicated events that include distinguished guests and audiences of hundreds. The Deputy Chief of Staff will ensure the Department hosts well-run events. Center for Workforce Equity & Illinois Center for Education Equity – supporting special initiatives out of the Centers, particularly as it relates to partnership engagement. Strategic Positioning, Data, & Continuous Improvement Serve as a strategic advisor to the Senior Vice President, leading planning, prioritization, and execution of division-wide goals. Manage philanthropic, state, and federal grant budgets, project plans, and seeking grants Track key performance indicators and outcomes across initiatives Oversee day-to-day operations of the External Affairs Department, including agenda management, follow-up tracking, and decision documentation. Support compliance with applicable state laws, public records requirements, ethics rules, lobbying regulations, and system policies. Assist with budget planning, expenditure tracking, and reporting in accordance with public university and system guidelines. Communications, Reporting & Stakeholder Engagement Serve as a primary point of coordination between the External Affairs Department, university leadership, system offices, and external stakeholders. Draft and review internal reports and materials Support transparency and accountability through timely reporting and data-driven updates. Manage the SVP’s calendar, schedule, and communications Minimum Qualifications Must establish Illinois residency within 180 calendar days of the start date Bachelor’s degree. A total of three (3) years (36 months) in education, training and/or work experience in the area of specialization inherent to the position. (Note: Master’s Degree in an area consistent with the duties of the position may be substituted for one (1) year of work experience. Based on position requirements, additional education, training, and/or work experience in the area of specialization inherent to the position, may be required. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s degree required; 3–5 years of progressively complex experience in a public university, government agency, system office, or related public-sector or non-profit environment. Strong understanding of public governance, political processes, and organizational dynamics. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with experience preparing materials for senior leaders and public officials. Excellent project management skills Experience in running well-organized, complex events Sound judgment, discretion, and attention to detail Relationship management and diplomacy Commitment to public higher education and service Experience working with or supporting governing boards, system offices, or elected officials. Master’s degree in public administration, public policy, higher education, business, or related field preferred. Strategic planning and execution Public-sector project management Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Additional Applicant Information Physical Requirement/ Demands Work Environment May require occasional evening or weekend work to support legislative sessions, board meetings, or university events. Periodic travel may be required for meetings with legislators, system offices, or external partners. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter References Optional Documents If you are interested in attending CSU, please complete our graduate or undergraduate form, and we will send you admissions information. Copyright © 2009 All Rights Reserved. Chicago State University | 9501 South King Drive, Chicago, Illinois 60628-1598 | (773) 995-2000 Emergency and Weather Updates | Swine Flu Updates | Exercise Your Right to Vote | Higher Learning Commission Mark of Affiliation | Campus Security Report | Whistle Blower Protections | Report A Site Problem | For Those With Disabilities | The university's policy is to be in full compliance with all federal and state nondiscrimination and equal opportunity laws, orders and regulations. Privacy Policy | Chicago State University is an Equal Opportunity/ Affirmative Action Employer (PDF) | These pages are best viewed with Internet Explorer 7, Netscape 7.1, Firefox 3.5.x, Safari 3.1.2, Chrome 3.0.1 and later browsers. | Undergraduate Admissions' Information | Exercise Your Right to Vote To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://chicagostate.peopleadmin.com/pools/15853": {
      "title": "Chicago State University Applicant Portal Site",
      "description": "Chicago State University Applicant Portal Site Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Part-Time Lecturer (Art & Design) (Pool) Bookmark this Pool | Print Preview | Apply for this Pool Pool Details Pool Information for the Posting Pool Number Pool Name Part-Time Lecturer (Art & Design) Faculty Rank Lecturer Class Code C6139 Is Tenured/ Tenure Track No Full-time/ Part-time Part-time Job Description Summary The budgeted salary for this position is typically $1,000 per credit hour . This position is ineligible for health, dental, and life insurance benefits through Chicago State University. Chicago State University ( CSU ), is the oldest public university in the Chicago metropolitan area. Chicago State University is Illinois’ only four-year U.S. Department of Education-designated Predominantly Black Institution ( PBI ). CSU serves over 1,500 undergraduate students and nearly 900 graduate students. The university is a nationally accredited university with five colleges in Arts and Sciences, Business, Education, Health Sciences and Pharmacy and proudly supports a diverse and non-traditional student population that hails from 28 countries and 36 states. Discover the latest advancements and milestones achieved by CSU in our Annual Report : https://www.csu.edu/president/annual_report.htm . The Department of Art & Design at Chicago State University is looking to fill one adjunct teaching position for the Fall 2014 semester. WEB PAGE DESIGN : This course is an introduction to web page design taught at the junior level and has pre-requisities of Graphic Designs I, Illustrator/Photoshop and Typography, as well as Drawing I and 2 D Design. Required Education Must have an MFA Required Knowledge, Skills and Abilities In addition to having an MFA in a related design discipline, a successful candidate will have the following skills and experience: Ability to teach Web Page Design on a MAC platform Teaching experience at the college/university level in web page design Sound knowledge of the Adobe CS5 Suite A portfolio of work in web page design *The ability to work with a diverse student population Preferred Qualifications Posting Information Open Date 02/21/2025 Close Date 06/30/2025 Pass Message Fail Message Special Instructions to Applicants For additional information contact Lillian Kay Dawson at ldawson@csu.edu or (773)995-3984 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter References Optional Documents If you are interested in attending CSU, please complete our graduate or undergraduate form, and we will send you admissions information. Copyright © 2009 All Rights Reserved. Chicago State University | 9501 South King Drive, Chicago, Illinois 60628-1598 | (773) 995-2000 Emergency and Weather Updates | Swine Flu Updates | Exercise Your Right to Vote | Higher Learning Commission Mark of Affiliation | Campus Security Report | Whistle Blower Protections | Report A Site Problem | For Those With Disabilities | The university's policy is to be in full compliance with all federal and state nondiscrimination and equal opportunity laws, orders and regulations. Privacy Policy | Chicago State University is an Equal Opportunity/ Affirmative Action Employer (PDF) | These pages are best viewed with Internet Explorer 7, Netscape 7.1, Firefox 3.5.x, Safari 3.1.2, Chrome 3.0.1 and later browsers. | Undergraduate Admissions' Information | Exercise Your Right to Vote To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://chicagostate.peopleadmin.com/postings/16961": {
      "title": "Chicago State University Applicant Portal Site | Assistant Professor of Educational Leadership and Administration",
      "description": "Chicago State University Applicant Portal Site | Assistant Professor of Educational Leadership and Administration Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor of Educational Leadership and Administration Bookmark this Hiring-Authorization Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number F260065P Open Date 07/20/2026 Close Date 08/07/2026 Faculty Rank Assistant Professor Title Assistant Professor of Educational Leadership and Administration Salary $71,000 Annual Benefits This position is eligible for health, dental, life insurance and other benefits through Chicago State University. Click here for a complete list of benefits: https://csu.edu/humanresources/benefits.htm Is Tenured/ Tenure Track Yes Full-time/ Part-time Full-time Job Description Summary The Educational Leadership program at Chicago State University invites applications from well-qualified candidates to fill a tenure-track faculty position beginning August 16, 2026. The selected individual will teach Educational Leadership courses in PreK-12 School Leadership, Higher Education Administration, and Instructional Leadership. Required Education Earned doctorate in Educational Leadership or related Education or Learning fields. Subject to administrative approval, applicants who are ABD may be considered provided they can demonstrate documented progress toward completion and the ability to successfully defend their dissertation within a timeframe deemed reasonable by institutional leadership. Required Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Demonstrated experience in and/or commitment to advancing equity initiatives within an educational setting and the integration of pedagogies/alignment with the Illinois Culturally Responsive Teaching and Leading ( CRTL ) standards. Preferred Qualifications Experience with collaborative, participatory, community, or action research methodologies and practices. Experience with assistive and instructional technology Experience teaching across modalities, including online, virtual/hybrid, and in-person/on-campus. Expertise in teaching literacy, math, and practicum courses required in our programs. Experience working with students with high and low-incidence disability designations at the PreK-22 level. Expertise in Practice-Based Teaching ( PBT ) and High-Leverage and Evidence-based Practices (HLPs) Special Requirements Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Transcripts Sample Syllabi List of (3) References Optional Documents Certification If you are interested in attending CSU, please complete our graduate or undergraduate form, and we will send you admissions information. Copyright © 2009 All Rights Reserved. Chicago State University | 9501 South King Drive, Chicago, Illinois 60628-1598 | (773) 995-2000 Emergency and Weather Updates | Swine Flu Updates | Exercise Your Right to Vote | Higher Learning Commission Mark of Affiliation | Campus Security Report | Whistle Blower Protections | Report A Site Problem | For Those With Disabilities | The university's policy is to be in full compliance with all federal and state nondiscrimination and equal opportunity laws, orders and regulations. Privacy Policy | Chicago State University is an Equal Opportunity/ Affirmative Action Employer (PDF) | These pages are best viewed with Internet Explorer 7, Netscape 7.1, Firefox 3.5.x, Safari 3.1.2, Chrome 3.0.1 and later browsers. | Undergraduate Admissions' Information | Exercise Your Right to Vote To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://chicagostate.peopleadmin.com/pools/15885": {
      "title": "Chicago State University Applicant Portal Site",
      "description": "Chicago State University Applicant Portal Site Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Part-Time Lecturer - Public Relations (Pool) Bookmark this Pool | Print Preview | Apply for this Pool Pool Details Pool Information for the Posting Pool Number Pool Name Part-Time Lecturer - Public Relations Faculty Rank Lecturer Class Code C6139 Is Tenured/ Tenure Track No Full-time/ Part-time Job Description Summary The budgeted salary for this position is typically $1,000 per credit hour . This position is ineligible for health, dental, and life insurance benefits through Chicago State University. Chicago State University ( CSU ), is the oldest public university in the Chicago metropolitan area. Chicago State University is Illinois’ only four-year U.S. Department of Education-designated Predominantly Black Institution ( PBI ). CSU serves over 1,500 undergraduate students and nearly 900 graduate students. The university is a nationally accredited university with five colleges in Arts and Sciences, Business, Education, Health Sciences and Pharmacy and proudly supports a diverse and non-traditional student population that hails from 28 countries and 36 states. Discover the latest advancements and milestones achieved by CSU in our Annual Report : https://www.csu.edu/president/annual_report.htm . The Program in Communications, Media Arts and Theatre seeks applicants for a part-time, non-tenure track lecturer to teach undergraduate courses in Public Relations. Primary duties include teaching 1 or 2 courses during a 4.5 month semester. Faculty members are expected to teach, develop syllabi and teaching materials related to courses taught, and hold regular office hours. Faculty are hired, evaluated, and retained on the basis of conditions covered in the Union Contract. Required Education An MA or PhD in Public Relations, Journalism, Communications or a related field, is required. Required Knowledge, Skills and Abilities We are seeking who is capable of teaching undergraduate courses covering the theory and practice of Public Relations. Professional experience in a public relations position is also preferred. Preferred Qualifications University level teaching experience preferred Posting Information Open Date 02/21/2025 Close Date 06/30/2025 Pass Message Fail Message Special Instructions to Applicants Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Transcripts Optional Documents If you are interested in attending CSU, please complete our graduate or undergraduate form, and we will send you admissions information. Copyright © 2009 All Rights Reserved. Chicago State University | 9501 South King Drive, Chicago, Illinois 60628-1598 | (773) 995-2000 Emergency and Weather Updates | Swine Flu Updates | Exercise Your Right to Vote | Higher Learning Commission Mark of Affiliation | Campus Security Report | Whistle Blower Protections | Report A Site Problem | For Those With Disabilities | The university's policy is to be in full compliance with all federal and state nondiscrimination and equal opportunity laws, orders and regulations. Privacy Policy | Chicago State University is an Equal Opportunity/ Affirmative Action Employer (PDF) | These pages are best viewed with Internet Explorer 7, Netscape 7.1, Firefox 3.5.x, Safari 3.1.2, Chrome 3.0.1 and later browsers. | Undergraduate Admissions' Information | Exercise Your Right to Vote To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
