    "https://chicagostate.peopleadmin.com/postings/16624": {
      "title": "Chicago State University Applicant Portal Site | Assistant Professor of Psychology and Counseling",
      "description": "Chicago State University Applicant Portal Site | Assistant Professor of Psychology and Counseling Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor of Psychology and Counseling Bookmark this Hiring-Authorization Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number F260051P Open Date 03/16/2026 Close Date 03/23/2026 Faculty Rank Assistant Professor Title Assistant Professor of Psychology and Counseling Salary $65,000 Annual Benefits This position is eligible for health, dental, life insurance and other benefits through Chicago State University. Click here for a complete list of benefits: https://csu.edu/humanresources/benefits.htm Is Tenured/ Tenure Track Yes Full-time/ Part-time Full-time Job Description Summary All faculty positions are governed by the tenets of a collective bargaining agreement. Faculty are hired, evaluated, retained, promoted, and tenured on the basis of conditions covered in the union contract. Primary duties include teaching and related activities assigned during a 9- or 12-month year. It is expected that each faculty member engages in all three activities of teaching, research/creative activities and service. Teaching: faculty members are expected to teach 4 to 8 credit courses per year; develop syllabi, teaching materials (ability to organize, analyze and present knowledge or materials) related to courses taught; and collaborate with other faculty in the development of new courses and/or programs. Some disciplines require discipline specific certifications and/or licensure in the field for practice or functioning within the State of Illinois; degree specific course work and/or graduate degrees in the discipline. In addition, faculty advise students, participate in professional development activities, as well as engage in assessment activities related to accreditation and program evaluation. Research: Faculty members are expected to engage in research and/or creative activity germane to an academic discipline, which results in submissions and material as works in refereed, professional and/or general readership publications; submit and receive externally awarded grants; submit proposals for presentations at academic and professional conferences; or engage in creative pursuits if in a creative, performing or theatrical arts discipline. Service: Faculty members are expected to serve on committees, programs, and/or special task forces at the department, college, university, professional and community levels; assume leadership roles over time and as they increase in rank. These activities are not for compensation and have a relationship to the employee’s assigned responsibilities and to the university. Required Education Earned terminal degree from an accredited university. Meets tenure and/or rank requirements from a discipline within the unit as defined by the collective bargaining unit; Previous academic experience at a four year college or university: 5 or more years teaching experience as determined by rank criteria; Previous professional experience related to the discipline: 5 or more years as determined by the discipline and rank criteria; and Record of scholarly research, creative activity in a discipline as well as receipt of competitive grants or externally awarded funding. Required Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Chicago State University seeks a Counselor Educator from a CACREP approved doctoral program. Preferred Qualifications Experience in using modern teaching approaches that incorporate active learning and technology. Experience as a school counselor or clinical mental health counselor with appropriate licensure/certification, in mentoring graduate students in research, teaching graduate students in a counseling program, and/or working with students from diverse backgrounds is preferred. Women and diverse applicants are strongly encouraged to apply. Record of potential for scholarly research as well as potential for receipt of competitive grants or externally awarded funding. Special Requirements Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents If you are interested in attending CSU, please complete our graduate or undergraduate form, and we will send you admissions information. Copyright © 2009 All Rights Reserved. Chicago State University | 9501 South King Drive, Chicago, Illinois 60628-1598 | (773) 995-2000 Emergency and Weather Updates | Swine Flu Updates | Exercise Your Right to Vote | Higher Learning Commission Mark of Affiliation | Campus Security Report | Whistle Blower Protections | Report A Site Problem | For Those With Disabilities | The university's policy is to be in full compliance with all federal and state nondiscrimination and equal opportunity laws, orders and regulations. Privacy Policy | Chicago State University is an Equal Opportunity/ Affirmative Action Employer (PDF) | These pages are best viewed with Internet Explorer 7, Netscape 7.1, Firefox 3.5.x, Safari 3.1.2, Chrome 3.0.1 and later browsers. | Undergraduate Admissions' Information | Exercise Your Right to Vote To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://chicagostate.peopleadmin.com/postings/17043": {
      "title": "Chicago State University Applicant Portal Site | Teacher Assistant Infant-Toddler-Two (IT2)",
      "description": "Chicago State University Applicant Portal Site | Teacher Assistant Infant-Toddler-Two (IT2) Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Teacher Assistant Infant-Toddler-Two (IT2) Bookmark this Hiring-Authorization Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number S26337P Posting Date Closing Date Title Child Care Assistant Working Title Teacher Assistant Infant-Toddler-Two (IT2) Salary Range $20.51 Per Hour Employee Class Civil Service Department Office of the Dean of Education Full-time/ Part-time Full-time Specialization Early Childhood Education Infant-Toddler development, care and teaching knowledge and experience. Hours Per Week 37.5 Standard Work Week Monday - Friday Benefits This position is eligible for health, dental, life insurance and other benefits through Chicago State University. Click here for a complete list of benefits: https://csu.edu/humanresources/benefits.htm Job Summary The Teacher Assistant IT2 position works in a collaborative co-teaching team model to provide high quality early care and learning experiences to children 3 months – 3 years old. In this role the person under the guidance of the teams lead plans and implements curriculum. Supports the implementation and completion of child development screenings and assessments. Engage in all family engagement activities such as home visits, conferences, etc. Adhere, to all licensing, funding and accreditation standards and compliance. Maintain, a safe, health nurturing and developmentally appropriate environment. Job Description Job Duties – Assistant Teacher (Infant/Toddler/Two-Year-Old Classroom) Collaborate with the lead teacher and co-teaching team to plan and implement developmentally appropriate curriculum and daily learning activities for children ages 3 months to 3 years. Support the delivery of high-quality early care and learning experiences that promote children’s social, emotional, cognitive, language, and physical development. Assist in observing children and documenting developmental progress to support ongoing assessments and child development screenings. Contribute to the implementation and completion of required child development screenings and assessments in collaboration with the teaching team. Foster warm, responsive relationships with children through nurturing interactions, positive guidance, and attentive caregiving routines. Assist with daily classroom routines including feeding, diapering, toileting, napping, and transitions while promoting children’s independence and well-being. Maintain a safe, clean, healthy, and developmentally appropriate classroom environment that supports active learning and exploration. Ensure all classroom practices comply with licensing regulations, program funding requirements, and accreditation standards. Support family engagement by participating in activities such as parent conferences, home visits, and family events as directed by the teaching team. Communicate respectfully and effectively with families to support children’s learning and development. Prepare and organize classroom materials, learning centers, and activities that reflect the planned curriculum. Work collaboratively with team members and program staff to maintain consistent classroom practices and a positive learning environment. Participate in required trainings, meetings, and professional development opportunities to enhance early childhood teaching practices. Follow program policies and procedures related to health, safety, supervision, and child protection. May be assigned as the temporary team lead in absence of the lead. Other duties as assigned an appropriate to the overall success of the program. Minimum Qualifications CREDENTIALS TO BE VERIFIED BY PLACEMENT OFFICER High school diploma or equivalent. Possession of credentials required by Illinois Department of Children and Family Services for employment as a Child Care Assistant. Preferred Qualifications 60 semester or 90 quarter hours (from accredited college or university) With 6 semester or 9 quarter credit hours in ECE , child development ot related course work. Must have or be working towards a IL Gateway Level 4 IT credential as indicated on IL Gateway PDR . . Have at least 1 year experience working with children birth – 5 years old Alternatively: Have a High School/ GED with a valid Infant Toddler CDA . Must have or be working towards a IL Gateway Level 2 IT credential as indicated on IL Gateway PDR . 1 year experience working with children birth – 5 years old. Associate Degree in ECE or Child Development with a Level 4 IL Gateway IT credential. 3 years experience in working with children birth – 5 in a child care or school setting. 1 year experience as an Early Head Start teacher. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Meet all University and DCFS hiring requirements, including background check and -Physical Examination Follow all DCFS licensing guidelines and Head Start Performance Standards Attend required training and professional development Additional Applicant Information Physical Requirement/ Demands The role requires significant physical stamina, with long periods of standing, walking between the kitchen and classrooms, and regularly lifting and moving items. Must be able to physically interact with children, including talk, hear, sit, stand, walk; use hands to finger, handle or feel objects, tools, or controls; reach with hands and arms; and stoop, kneel, crouch,or crawl and lift and or move items of up to 50 pounds Work Environment Typical early childhood center classroom environment. Classroom are designed to be child centered with child size furnished and equipment per developmentally appropriate per age group. Outdoor spaces with child size equipment and campus walks as permissible per weather and/or safety conditions. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). What is the highest level of education attained? GED High School Diploma Associates Degree Bachelors Degree Masters Degree PHD How many years of experience do you have in this type of position? 0-1 1-3 3-5 5-7 7+ Do you have an Illinois Gateway Infant-Toddler credential? Yes No Do you agree to a IL DCFS background check that includes finger printing, criminal history, child abuse and neglect, sex offender and possible FBI check? Yes No Do you have experience working with young children birth-3 years old? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of (3) References Optional Documents References Transcripts Letters of Reference If you are interested in attending CSU, please complete our graduate or undergraduate form, and we will send you admissions information. Copyright © 2009 All Rights Reserved. Chicago State University | 9501 South King Drive, Chicago, Illinois 60628-1598 | (773) 995-2000 Emergency and Weather Updates | Swine Flu Updates | Exercise Your Right to Vote | Higher Learning Commission Mark of Affiliation | Campus Security Report | Whistle Blower Protections | Report A Site Problem | For Those With Disabilities | The university's policy is to be in full compliance with all federal and state nondiscrimination and equal opportunity laws, orders and regulations. Privacy Policy | Chicago State University is an Equal Opportunity/ Affirmative Action Employer (PDF) | These pages are best viewed with Internet Explorer 7, Netscape 7.1, Firefox 3.5.x, Safari 3.1.2, Chrome 3.0.1 and later browsers. | Undergraduate Admissions' Information | Exercise Your Right to Vote To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://chicagostate.peopleadmin.com/postings/16519": {
      "title": "Chicago State University Applicant Portal Site | Assistant Professor of Art History",
      "description": "Chicago State University Applicant Portal Site | Assistant Professor of Art History Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor of Art History Bookmark this Hiring-Authorization Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number F260046P Open Date 01/26/2026 Close Date 03/23/2026 Faculty Rank Assistant Professor Title Assistant Professor of Art History Salary $63,000 Annual Benefits This position is eligible for health, dental, life insurance and other benefits through Chicago State University. Click here for a complete list of benefits: https://csu.edu/humanresources/benefits.htm . Is Tenured/ Tenure Track Yes Full-time/ Part-time Full-time Job Description Summary Chicago State University ( CSU ), is the oldest public university in the Chicago metropolitan area. Chicago State University is Illinois’ only four-year U.S. Department of Education-designated Predominantly Black Institution ( PBI ). CSU serves over 1,500 undergraduate students and nearly 900 graduate students. The university is a nationally accredited university with five colleges in Arts and Sciences, Business, Education, Health Sciences and Pharmacy and proudly supports a diverse and non-traditional student population that hails from 28 countries and 36 states. Discover the latest advancements and milestones achieved by CSU in our Annual Report : https://www.csu.edu/president/annual_report.htm . Chicago State University Department of Art and Design invites applications for a 9-month, tenure-track position as Assistant Professor of Art History, beginning August 2026. We are looking for a faculty member who is committed to excellence in teaching, scholarly research, and student success in a diverse and inclusive environment. Candidates should demonstrate a strong commitment to dynamic and innovative undergraduate teaching and support activities that encourage unique learning opportunities in our University Gallery program as well as the classroom. Additional responsibilities include maintaining an active program of scholarly research, supporting student mentorship and professional development along with department and university service. Required Education The desired applicant must have a Ph.D. in Art History or a related equivalent subject. Required Knowledge, Skills and Abilities The successful candidate will develop curriculum and teach a range of art history courses, from Ancient and Medieval through Modern and Contemporary subject matter, in a BA Degree program with degree options in 2D & 3D Studio Art, Design, and PK-12 Art Education. The candidate will also develop and coordinate course curriculum for Introduction to Visual Art, a general education course for non-majors. Preferred Qualifications Experience working with a diverse population of students. Several years of professional practice in the field. Preference will be given to candidates that also have gallery and museum curatorial experience and/or studio art practice. Demonstrated interest in interdisciplinary collaboration and/or community engagement is also highly recommended. Special Requirements Sample syllabi for relevant courses and addition examples of research must be emailed to Thomas Lucas, tlucas22@csu.edu and John Smith, john.smith@csu.edu College level teaching experience is required. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae References Research Agenda Teaching Philosophy Letters of Reference Sample Syllabi Optional Documents If you are interested in attending CSU, please complete our graduate or undergraduate form, and we will send you admissions information. Copyright © 2009 All Rights Reserved. Chicago State University | 9501 South King Drive, Chicago, Illinois 60628-1598 | (773) 995-2000 Emergency and Weather Updates | Swine Flu Updates | Exercise Your Right to Vote | Higher Learning Commission Mark of Affiliation | Campus Security Report | Whistle Blower Protections | Report A Site Problem | For Those With Disabilities | The university's policy is to be in full compliance with all federal and state nondiscrimination and equal opportunity laws, orders and regulations. Privacy Policy | Chicago State University is an Equal Opportunity/ Affirmative Action Employer (PDF) | These pages are best viewed with Internet Explorer 7, Netscape 7.1, Firefox 3.5.x, Safari 3.1.2, Chrome 3.0.1 and later browsers. | Undergraduate Admissions' Information | Exercise Your Right to Vote To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://chicagostate.peopleadmin.com/pools/15865": {
      "title": "Chicago State University Applicant Portal Site",
      "description": "Chicago State University Applicant Portal Site Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Part-Time Lecturer/Art & Design/ Ceramics (Pool) Bookmark this Pool | Print Preview | Apply for this Pool Pool Details Pool Information for the Posting Pool Number Pool Name Part-Time Lecturer/Art & Design/ Ceramics Faculty Rank Lecturer Class Code C6136 Is Tenured/ Tenure Track No Full-time/ Part-time Part-time Job Description Summary The budgeted salary for this position is typically $1,000 per credit hour . This position is ineligible for health, dental, and life insurance benefits through Chicago State University. Chicago State University ( CSU ), is the oldest public university in the Chicago metropolitan area. Chicago State University is Illinois’ only four-year U.S. Department of Education-designated Predominantly Black Institution ( PBI ). CSU serves over 1,500 undergraduate students and nearly 900 graduate students. The university is a nationally accredited university with five colleges in Arts and Sciences, Business, Education, Health Sciences and Pharmacy and proudly supports a diverse and non-traditional student population that hails from 28 countries and 36 states. Discover the latest advancements and milestones achieved by CSU in our Annual Report : https://www.csu.edu/president/annual_report.htm . Duties: Teaching Ceramics I or upper level ceramics courses, II, III , and IV stacked. Mixing clay, loading, unloading and firing kilns. Working cooperatively with other ceramics lecturers in coordination of the facility. Required Education MFA in a related art discipline Required Knowledge, Skills and Abilities •Ability to teach hand building and throwing techniques •Ability to work with a diverse population of students •Ability to work collaboratively with the faculty member in charge of the Ceramics studio •Professional work must reflect a high level of technical ability and an understanding of and an interest in contemporary issues in the field of ceramics and/or the broader field of art •Experience mixing clay, loading and unloading work, and firing electric and gas kilns Preferred Qualifications •Experience teaching throwing and hand building techniques simultaneously in the same semester •Teaching experience at a college level •Exhibition record in the field is expected Posting Information Open Date 02/21/2025 Close Date 06/30/2025 Pass Message Fail Message Special Instructions to Applicants Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Teaching Philosophy References Optional Documents If you are interested in attending CSU, please complete our graduate or undergraduate form, and we will send you admissions information. Copyright © 2009 All Rights Reserved. Chicago State University | 9501 South King Drive, Chicago, Illinois 60628-1598 | (773) 995-2000 Emergency and Weather Updates | Swine Flu Updates | Exercise Your Right to Vote | Higher Learning Commission Mark of Affiliation | Campus Security Report | Whistle Blower Protections | Report A Site Problem | For Those With Disabilities | The university's policy is to be in full compliance with all federal and state nondiscrimination and equal opportunity laws, orders and regulations. Privacy Policy | Chicago State University is an Equal Opportunity/ Affirmative Action Employer (PDF) | These pages are best viewed with Internet Explorer 7, Netscape 7.1, Firefox 3.5.x, Safari 3.1.2, Chrome 3.0.1 and later browsers. | Undergraduate Admissions' Information | Exercise Your Right to Vote To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
