    "https://chicagostate.peopleadmin.com/postings/15830": {
      "title": "Chicago State University Applicant Portal Site | Part-Time Lecturer/Adjunct (Health Studies)",
      "description": "Chicago State University Applicant Portal Site | Part-Time Lecturer/Adjunct (Health Studies) Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Part-Time Lecturer/Adjunct (Health Studies) Bookmark this Hiring-Authorization Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. -The Candidate must hold at least an MPH from an accredited institution (CHES/MCHES) preferred with practical experience in public health or research in a related field to teach at the undergraduate level. -The Candidate must hold a PHD from an accredited institution (CHES/MCHES) preferred with extensive practical experience in public health or research in a related field, to teach at the graduate level. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number F240001P Open Date 08/15/2023 Close Date Faculty Rank Lecturer Title Part-Time Lecturer/Adjunct (Health Studies) Salary The salary for this position is $1,000 per credit hour. Benefits This position is ineligible for health, dental, and life insurance benefits through Chicago State University. Is Tenured/ Tenure Track No Full-time/ Part-time Part-time Job Description Summary Chicago State University ( CSU ), is the oldest public university in the Chicago metropolitan area. Chicago State University is Illinois’ only four-year U.S. Department of Education-designated Predominantly Black Institution ( PBI ). CSU serves over 1,500 undergraduate students and nearly 900 graduate students. The university is a nationally accredited university with five colleges in Arts and Sciences, Business, Education, Health Sciences and Pharmacy and proudly supports a diverse and non-traditional student population that hails from 28 countries and 36 states. Discover the latest advancements and milestones achieved by CSU in our Annual Report : https://www.csu.edu/president/annual_report.htm . Seeking an Adjunct faculty member to teach undergraduate or graduate level courses in Public Health. The position requires expertise in at least one area of public health, such as epidemiology, health policy and management, biostatistics, environmental health, and social and behavioral sciences. The adjunct faculty member will adhere to all university and academic policies and assigned duties, contribute to the development of course content, assess student learning, participate in program activities, provide student support, attend trainings, maintain accurate records of student’s academic progress, be available via phone, email, zoom, LMS and during office hours, and support the overall mission, vision and values of the public health program. Required Education - Master’s degree in public health or a related field, MPH , PhD preferred. - CHES / MCHES preferred not required. Required Knowledge, Skills and Abilities The position requires expertise in at least one area of public health, such as epidemiology, health policy and management, biostatistics, environmental health, and social and behavioral sciences. TheCandidate must also possess strong communication, presentation skills and teaching skills. Preferred Qualifications - Master’s degree in public health or a related field, MPH , PhD preferred. - CHES / MCHES preferred not required. Special Requirements Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How many years of experience do you have in this type of position? 0-1 1-3 3-5 5-7 7+ * What is your highest level of completed education? High School/GED Bachelor's Degree Master's Degree PhD * Do you hold a CHES or MCHES certification? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Curriculum Vitae References Transcripts Course Proposal Certification If you are interested in attending CSU, please complete our graduate or undergraduate form, and we will send you admissions information. Copyright © 2009 All Rights Reserved. Chicago State University | 9501 South King Drive, Chicago, Illinois 60628-1598 | (773) 995-2000 Emergency and Weather Updates | Swine Flu Updates | Exercise Your Right to Vote | Higher Learning Commission Mark of Affiliation | Campus Security Report | Whistle Blower Protections | Report A Site Problem | For Those With Disabilities | The university's policy is to be in full compliance with all federal and state nondiscrimination and equal opportunity laws, orders and regulations. Privacy Policy | Chicago State University is an Equal Opportunity/ Affirmative Action Employer (PDF) | These pages are best viewed with Internet Explorer 7, Netscape 7.1, Firefox 3.5.x, Safari 3.1.2, Chrome 3.0.1 and later browsers. | Undergraduate Admissions' Information | Exercise Your Right to Vote To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://chicagostate.peopleadmin.com/pools/15860": {
      "title": "Chicago State University Applicant Portal Site",
      "description": "Chicago State University Applicant Portal Site Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Part-Time Lecturer (Sociology) (Pool) Bookmark this Pool | Print Preview | Apply for this Pool Pool Details Pool Information for the Posting Pool Number Pool Name Part-Time Lecturer (Sociology) Faculty Rank Lecturer Class Code C6139 Is Tenured/ Tenure Track No Full-time/ Part-time Part-time Job Description Summary The budgeted salary for this position is typically $1,000 per credit hour . This position is ineligible for health, dental, and life insurance benefits through Chicago State University. Chicago State University ( CSU ), is the oldest public university in the Chicago metropolitan area. Chicago State University is Illinois’ only four-year U.S. Department of Education-designated Predominantly Black Institution ( PBI ). CSU serves over 1,500 undergraduate students and nearly 900 graduate students. The university is a nationally accredited university with five colleges in Arts and Sciences, Business, Education, Health Sciences and Pharmacy and proudly supports a diverse and non-traditional student population that hails from 28 countries and 36 states. Discover the latest advancements and milestones achieved by CSU in our Annual Report : https://www.csu.edu/president/annual_report.htm . Part-time teaching position in sociology. All faculty positions are governed by the tenets of a collective bargaining agreement. Faculty are hired, evaluated, and retained on the basis of conditions covered in the union contract. Primary duties include teaching and related activities assigned during a term of 4.5 months. It is expected that each faculty member engages in teaching and teaching-related activities. Non-tenure track faculty report to a department chairperson or director. Teaching: faculty members are expected to teach; develop syllabi and teaching materials (ability to organize, analyze, and present knowledge or materials) related to courses taught. Some disciplines require discipline specific certifications and/or licensure in the field for practice or functioning within the State of Illinois; degree specific course work and/or graduate degrees in the discipline. Required Education Master of Arts in Sociology; completed graduate degrees in related fields considered. Required Knowledge, Skills and Abilities The ability of a variety of introductory and advanced level sociology courses. The successful applicant must be prepared to teach new preparations. Preferred Qualifications Applicants must be comfortable teaching a variety of traditional and non-traditional students from diverse educational and cultural backgrounds. Posting Information Open Date 02/21/2025 Close Date 06/30/2025 Pass Message Fail Message Special Instructions to Applicants Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents If you are interested in attending CSU, please complete our graduate or undergraduate form, and we will send you admissions information. Copyright © 2009 All Rights Reserved. Chicago State University | 9501 South King Drive, Chicago, Illinois 60628-1598 | (773) 995-2000 Emergency and Weather Updates | Swine Flu Updates | Exercise Your Right to Vote | Higher Learning Commission Mark of Affiliation | Campus Security Report | Whistle Blower Protections | Report A Site Problem | For Those With Disabilities | The university's policy is to be in full compliance with all federal and state nondiscrimination and equal opportunity laws, orders and regulations. Privacy Policy | Chicago State University is an Equal Opportunity/ Affirmative Action Employer (PDF) | These pages are best viewed with Internet Explorer 7, Netscape 7.1, Firefox 3.5.x, Safari 3.1.2, Chrome 3.0.1 and later browsers. | Undergraduate Admissions' Information | Exercise Your Right to Vote To ensure the security of your data, you will be