    "https://chicagostate.peopleadmin.com/postings/17023": {
      "title": "Chicago State University Applicant Portal Site",
      "description": "Chicago State University Applicant Portal Site | Data Manager Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Data Manager Bookmark this Hiring-Authorization Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number S26330P Posting Date 02/19/2026 Closing Date 04/30/2026 Title Educational Program Evaluation Coordinator Working Title Data Manager Salary Range $46,500 Annual Employee Class Civil Service Department Office of the Dean of Education Full-time/ Part-time Full-time Specialization Experience with data warehousing, SQL , report writer tools (Microsoft Report Writer / Power BI), advance excel functionality (Power Query, DAX ) and Share Point. Hours Per Week 37.5 Standard Work Week Monday - Friday Benefits This position is eligible for health, dental, life insurance and other benefits through Chicago State University. Click here for a complete list of benefits: https://csu.edu/humanresources/benefits.htm Job Summary This position provides professional administrative services to the Dean, Department Heads and faculty by providing organized data for data analysis, accreditation, and other reporting purposes. Job Description Data entry and maintenance of databases housing score reporting mandated by state, regional and national governance Bodies as well as the College of Education for the purposes of accreditation, i.e., Illinois State Board of Education ( ISBE ) content and Educational Teacher Performance Assessment (EdTPA) scores, Disposition Scores, and Student Teaching Observation Tool. Data entry and maintenance of student information database which includes all student academic and program performance data. Collaborate with faculty identify key indicators for the Unit Assessment System ( UAS ) Use the database to generate aggregated and disaggregated student reports for faculty analysis. Use Qualtrics to obtain data necessary for feedback and to inform decisions and operations in the College of Education. Coordinate database system to track student progress in the departments for CAEP accreditation review, including Specialty Program Area ( SPA ) reporting. Aggregate data reports of faculty teaching evaluations. Using information and guidance provided by the Quality Assurance Committees, generate assessment reports for faculty analysis. Track, chart and generate data from Field-Base and Partnership initiatives for programmatic analysis. Create and monitor electronic survey systems for the COE including the Office of Field Placement and Outreach. Use Statistical Program i.e., Social Sciences ( SPSS ) to accomplish the creation and organized sharing of student data. Serve as a resource in monthly Dean Council and Teacher. Education Advisory Council ( TEAC ). Provide an annual review and audit of shared drive used to collect evidence. Consult in departmental assessment meetings. Consult on necessary redesigns of all reports. Design and facilitate inter-rater reliability workshops. Other Duties Assigned by the Dean Minimum Qualifications Bachelor degree in an educational or related field with a minimum of two courses in statistics. Two (2) years (24 months) of educational and/or other research experience. Illinois residency is required within 180 days of employment. Preferred Qualifications Data management: 1 year (Preferred) Knowledge, Skills and Abilities An ability to communicate technical details to non-technical faculty and staff. Demonstrated leadership ability. Exceptional communication and interpersonal skills. Strong commitment to quality education, with special sensitivity to the needs of minority students. Exceptional computer skills. Additional Applicant Information Physical Requirement/ Demands Work Environment Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume List of (3) References Optional Documents Cover Letter If you are interested in attending CSU, please complete our graduate or undergraduate form, and we will send you admissions information. Copyright © 2009 All Rights Reserved. Chicago State University | 9501 South King Drive, Chicago, Illinois 60628-1598 | (773) 995-2000 Emergency and Weather Updates | Swine Flu Updates | Exercise Your Right to Vote | Higher Learning Commission Mark of Affiliation | Campus Security Report | Whistle Blower Protections | Report A Site Problem | For Those With Disabilities | The university's policy is to be in full compliance with all federal and state nondiscrimination and equal opportunity laws, orders and regulations. Privacy Policy | Chicago State University is an Equal Opportunity/ Affirmative Action Employer (PDF) | These pages are best viewed with Internet Explorer 7, Netscape 7.1, Firefox 3.5.x, Safari 3.1.2, Chrome 3.0.1 and later browsers. | Undergraduate Admissions' Information | Exercise Your Right to Vote To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
