    "https://chicagostate.peopleadmin.com/pools/15857": {
      "title": "Chicago State University Applicant Portal Site",
      "description": "Chicago State University Applicant Portal Site Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Part-Time Lecturer (Art & Design) (Pool) Bookmark this Pool | Print Preview | Apply for this Pool Pool Details Pool Information for the Posting Pool Number Pool Name Part-Time Lecturer (Art & Design) Faculty Rank Lecturer Class Code C6139 Is Tenured/ Tenure Track No Full-time/ Part-time Part-time Job Description Summary The budgeted salary for this position is typically $1,000 per credit hour . This position is ineligible for health, dental, and life insurance benefits through Chicago State University. Chicago State University ( CSU ), is the oldest public university in the Chicago metropolitan area. Chicago State University is Illinois’ only four-year U.S. Department of Education-designated Predominantly Black Institution ( PBI ). CSU serves over 1,500 undergraduate students and nearly 900 graduate students. The university is a nationally accredited university with five colleges in Arts and Sciences, Business, Education, Health Sciences and Pharmacy and proudly supports a diverse and non-traditional student population that hails from 28 countries and 36 states. Discover the latest advancements and milestones achieved by CSU in our Annual Report : https://www.csu.edu/president/annual_report.htm . Duties: Teaching “Introduction to Visual Art.” This is a lecture course for non-art majors and has the following course description. “Appreciation and analysis of art forms stressing terminology, technical procedures, composition, materials, and cultural and social influences.” Required Education M.A., M.F.A., or Ph.D in the visual arts or art history. Required Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Ability to teach an introduction to visual arts course in lecture format. Ability to use digital means to deliver instruction. Ability to engage students through multiple pedagogical strategies. Preferred Qualifications Teaching experience at the college legel in the fields of visual art or art history. Posting Information Open Date 02/21/2025 Close Date 06/30/2025 Pass Message Fail Message Special Instructions to Applicants Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter References Optional Documents If you are interested in attending CSU, please complete our graduate or undergraduate form, and we will send you admissions information. Copyright © 2009 All Rights Reserved. Chicago State University | 9501 South King Drive, Chicago, Illinois 60628-1598 | (773) 995-2000 Emergency and Weather Updates | Swine Flu Updates | Exercise Your Right to Vote | Higher Learning Commission Mark of Affiliation | Campus Security Report | Whistle Blower Protections | Report A Site Problem | For Those With Disabilities | The university's policy is to be in full compliance with all federal and state nondiscrimination and equal opportunity laws, orders and regulations. Privacy Policy | Chicago State University is an Equal Opportunity/ Affirmative Action Employer (PDF) | These pages are best viewed with Internet Explorer 7, Netscape 7.1, Firefox 3.5.x, Safari 3.1.2, Chrome 3.0.1 and later browsers. | Undergraduate Admissions' Information | Exercise Your Right to Vote To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
