    "https://chicagostate.peopleadmin.com/postings/17007": {
      "title": "Chicago State University Applicant Portal Site | Enrollment Specialist",
      "description": "Chicago State University Applicant Portal Site | Enrollment Specialist Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Enrollment Specialist Bookmark this Hiring-Authorization Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number S27400P Posting Date 08/25/2026 Closing Date Title Enrollment Specialist Working Title Enrollment Specialist Salary Range $47,500 Annual Employee Class Administrator Department Undergraduate Admissions Full-time/ Part-time Full-time Specialization Hours Per Week 40 Standard Work Week Monday-Friday Benefits This position is eligible for health, dental, life insurance and other benefits through Chicago State University. Click here for a complete list of benefits: https://csu.edu/humanresources/benefits.htm Job Summary Represent the university at recruitment events hosed by high schools, community colleges, community and social service agencies, local and regional businesses, faith-based organizations, and etc. In consultation with the director, use historical enrollment data to make decisions regarding travel to target markets to represent the university at recruitment events. Regularly counsels and advises prospective students, families and the general public regarding university policies, procedures, the admissions process, pre-college planning and general information such as financial aide, housing, registration and other student services. Independently conduct a comprehensive admission file review process and use additional holistic information to make judgement calls to determine admissions decisions for new students based on a set criteria established by the university. This holistic approach includes review of official high school and/or college transcripts, application, and standardized test scores for individual students going through the review process and review prospective students’ application files on a daily basis. Foster public and personal relationships between prospective students and families and the university. In consultation with the director plan on-off campus recruiting events, including open houses, information sessions, arrangement of group and individual tours, workshops and other activities/events. Counsels and advises prospective and admitted students on matters involving career opportunities, academic majors and courses. Assist in the production and distribution of recruitment materials including but not limited to brochures, pamphlets, newsletters, etc. to represent the office of admissions and the university. Generates personal inquiries through network and professional relationships. Evaluate and advise prospective students using a consultative process to best determine educational needs and position CSU as the school of choice. Maintain a minimum standard of outbound and follow-up prospective students. Achieve contact efficiency metrics and guide students through the online application process. Support application/registration events as applicable. Maintain accurate interactions with prospective students in CRM . Coordinate tour requests and support admissions activities (open house, cougar start u, etc.). Participate on departmental and university committees. Participate in professional development activities annually. Complete other projects and duties as assigned. Job Description This is a professional position responsible for increasing undergraduate enrollment through coordinated, planned and data driven recruitment practices. Responsible for representing Chicago State University at high school, community college, university programs and events across the Midwest Including travel within Illinois, Indiana, Iowa, Kentucky, Michigan, Minnesota, Missouri and Wisconsin: counseling families, prospective students and the general public on all aspects of the admissions process at Chicago State University; assisting with planning and implementation of university on-and-off campus programs; assisting with marketing and relationship-building activities through electronic correspondence and recruiting events; maintaining excellent public relations with prospective students and their families; making decisions regarding admission to the university; determining and implementing recruitment strategies in order to achieve enrollment goals; and assisting with other enrollment related services. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree Preferred Qualifications Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Must possess a passion for education and the ability to inspire our student population. Must be able to be a self-starter and work in a fast-paced environment. Outstanding communication and listening skills – both written and verbal. Skill in public speaking and delivering presentations to individuals and groups. Ability to analyze complex information and exercise sound judgement in making decisions. Ability to set priorities and complete assignments and tasks on time. Ability to operate personal computer with general understanding of application software and understanding of the internet and use of social media. Knowledge in Microsoft Suite of products. Ability to work a flexible schedule, evenings and weekends to accommodate students or departmental needs. This may include working more than 40 hours a week on occasion. Must have reliable transportation and valid driver’s license. Additional Applicant Information Physical Requirement/ Demands Frequently required to sit at a desk/workstation for a long period of time. Adaptability of long/non-traditional hours. Moderate lifting and carrying of supplies, files, etc. Ability to speak to and hear employees/clients via phone or in-person. Body motor skills sufficient to enable incumbent to move around the office environment. Ability to analyze data and other reports and make recommendations. Mental requirements include: compare, decide, direct, problem solve, analyze, instruct, interpret. Work Environment Office and conference room settings. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter References Optional Documents If you are interested in attending CSU, please complete our graduate or undergraduate form, and we will send you admissions information. Copyright © 2009 All Rights Reserved. Chicago State University | 9501 South King Drive, Chicago, Illinois 60628-1598 | (773) 995-2000 Emergency and Weather Updates | Swine Flu Updates | Exercise Your Right to Vote | Higher Learning Commission Mark of Affiliation | Campus Security Report | Whistle Blower Protections | Report A Site Problem | For Those With Disabilities | The university's policy is to be in full compliance with all federal and state nondiscrimination and equal opportunity laws, orders and regulations. Privacy Policy | Chicago State University is an Equal Opportunity/ Affirmative Action Employer (PDF) | These pages are best viewed with Internet Explorer 7, Netscape 7.1, Firefox 3.5.x, Safari 3.1.2, Chrome 3.0.1 and later browsers. | Undergraduate Admissions' Information | Exercise Your Right to Vote To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
